/**
 @file module.modulemap
 @brief Clang Module Map for ZephyrSys Swift-C Interoperability (Swift 6.3)

 This module map defines how Swift code can import and use C APIs from the
 ZephyrSys library and Zephyr RTOS. With Swift 6.3's enhanced C interoperability,
 this module enables bidirectional interop between Swift implementations and
 C interfaces.

 ## Swift 6.3 Features Supported

 This module map leverages Swift 6.3's embedded mode improvements:
 - @c functions that generate C-compatible symbols
 - @implementation attribute for existing C header implementations
 - Improved tolerance of C signature mismatches
 - Enhanced embedded Swift runtime support

 ## Module Structure

 The ZephyrSys module provides access to:
 - Zephyr RTOS C APIs through BridgingHeader.h
 - Swift-implemented C functions
 - Bidirectional Swift-C interoperability

 ## Usage Examples

 Swift code:
 ```swift
 import ZephyrSys

 // Use Zephyr APIs
 let device = device_get_binding("GPIO_0")
 k_sleep(K_MSEC(100))

 // Call Swift-implemented C functions
 zephyr_sys_init()
 ```

 C code:
 ```c
 #include "BridgingHeader.h"

 int main() {
     zephyr_sys_init();  // Calls Swift implementation
     return 0;
 }
 ```
 */

/**
 @brief ZephyrSys Module Definition (Swift 6.3 Enhanced)

 Defines the ZephyrSys module for bidirectional Swift-C interoperability.

 Module attributes:
 - umbrella header: Main bridging header with Zephyr APIs and C interface
 - link: Links against the ZephyrSys static library containing Swift objects
 - export *: Makes all symbols available to importing code
 */
module ZephyrSys {
  umbrella header "BridgingHeader.h"
  link "ZephyrSys"
  export *
}
